Article 41

In carrying out investigation duties, Civil Servant Investigators are authorized to:

a. receive, seek, collect and examine information or reports concerning criminal acts;
b. examine, seek and collect information regarding individuals or entities concerning the truth of acts committed in connection with criminal acts;
c. request information and evidence from individuals or entities in connection with criminal acts;
d. examine books, records and other documents concerning criminal acts;
e. conduct searches to obtain evidence of bookkeeping, records and other documents as well as conduct seizures of such evidence;
f. request the assistance of experts in the framework of carrying out criminal investigation duties;
g. order to stop, prohibit a person from leaving a room or place at the time the examination is in progress and examine the identity of the person and or documents carried as referred to in letter e of this Article;
h. take fingerprints and photograph a person related to a criminal act;
i. summon a person to be heard for their statement and examined as a suspect or witness;
j. terminate the investigation after receiving instructions from the POLRI investigator that there is insufficient evidence or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the POLRI investigator notify this matter to the public prosecutor, suspect or their family;
k. take other actions necessary for the smooth running of criminal investigation, according to law that can be accounted for.

